  {
    "episode_id": 74624,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74624.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to the Commonwealth Matters. I'm Richard Nelson, Executive Director of CPC. Thanks for joining us with us on today's program is Congressman James Comer. He's represented Kentucky's first district in Congress since 2016. He serves on the Committee on Education and Labor, the Committee on Agriculture, and he's also the ranking member on the Committee on Oversight and Reform. In fact, he is the GOP point person on that Committee. Congressman Comer, welcome to the program. Thanks for having me on. Hey, it's always good to get insight as to what's going on in Washington DC, especially from our very own congressman. You were my personal congressman for several years until I moved from the first district. I was over in Trig County recently moved up to Frankfurt, but I appreciate your on a personal level, your voice and your leadership in Congress. I know it's a tough place to be for a conservative. You're in the minority, but you have certainly not been quiet. when it comes to important issues facing the Commonwealth and facing the country. And often people will see you on Fox News and other news outlets weighing in on the important issues that they particularly because if you are being a ranking member on the committee on oversight and reform, could you speak briefly as to how important that is that committee?",
