  {
    "episode_id": 74624,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74624.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "I think the oversight committee will be the most high profile committee when the Republicans flip the house next year. So if the elections go as we hope, then the Republicans will be in the majority. We'll get a new speaker to the House. We don't have to put up with Nancy Pelosi before. That would start in January of 2023. The House Oversight Committee then will be the primary committee responsible for finally providing some type of oversight and or accountability to the Biden administration. So to be chairman of the, and I'll be chairman of the committee, to be chairman of that committee with Biden is president and all the problems that he's had from the debacle in Afghanistan to inflation to the lack of border security, not to mention his terrible policies, terrible social policies, energy policies and everything else. I think we'll have plenty of opportunities to message, to try to hold him accountable to get information to answer questions that people have about who's in charge of this agency, who made the decision to do what. And I'm really excited about that. The last Republican chairman when we were in the majority of the oversight committee was Trey Gout. So if you watch Fox News, you know, who Trey Gouty was, of course he did the Benghazi hearings again, Hillary Clinton back in the back of the day. So I'm really excited about it. The oversight committee also has jurisdiction over government operations. I'm real passionate about waste fraud abuse. All I see is waste fraud abuse up here and we're going to try to highlight programs that can be cut and or eliminated. We're going to try to bring a lot of programs that are being abused, whether it's fraud, like with the unemployment insurance being, you know, being such a disaster from a hacking standpoint and things like that. So lots of opportunities in oversight committee and I'm really looking forward to that opportunity.",
