    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "Well, the election a few weeks ago in Virginia and New Jersey, as much as anywhere, showed that a lot of the swing voters have swung back to the Republican Party. If you look at 2020, the demographic that stuck out most and prevented us from flipping the house and prevented the Senate from going Republican and obviously hurt President Trump were suburban women. And right now, if you poll suburban women there. And this is suburban women. So it's not like my district. What are their three big issues? Education and throughout my whole life. Democrats have uphold Republicans on education, especially with women. But if you remember what Terry McCulloch said, the parents don't have any right in a child's education and they just cater to the teachers union. We've seen that in Kentucky. The Democrat party continues to cater to the teachers union. They don't put the education of the child first front and center, then the teaching curriculum, the critical race theory, you know, the liberal indoctrination coming from a lot of public school teachers, especially on the post-secondary level. I think that they and in the virtual learning, you know, not having in-person school because the teachers union didn't want to go to in-person school because of COVID and all that. Parents are frustrated, especially the mothers, they're frustrated with the quality of public education. They know the Democrats have run the public education system for years and years and years and they're fed up with it. The next issue besides education, inflation, they see inflation every day and they realize that this is a direct result of Joe Biden's policies and the Democrat policies. And then lastly, in the suburbs, crimes on the And you got the Democrats trying to defund the police. You've got the lack of border security, which is creating, you know, droves of illegals coming in. You know, these, these illegals that come in, they don't end up on the border. They end up in the suburbs and in the cities, right? So the crime has gone up, you know, just a lot there just in places like Louisville too. So that issue leads me to believe if we can get that demographic back, then we'll be in pretty good shape histories on our side. And there's nothing I'm seeing other Biden administration that makes me think they're going to be able to turn it",
