    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Very interesting. We will find out in about a year from now whether or not Congress will be in Republican hands. So stay tuned. A lot of time between now and then. Congressman Comer, fiscal responsibility is one of your hallmark issues. You have been a fiscal hawk, I would say, while serving in Kentucky. in the legislature on many issues. But now you're in Congress, whole different ball game, much bigger budgets. A lot of money was just spent by Congress with the infrastructure bill. Congress passed the $1.2 trillion. That's trillion with the T past Congress. Of course, you voted against it. One thing I didn't wasn't aware of. You pointed this out. Less than 10% of the bill contained surface infrastructure like roads and bridges. And when you think infrastructure, that's what you're thinking, roads and bridges and things to maintain our transportation system. But that really wasn't the case, was it?",
