    "turn_text": "in the building materials sector of the economy, and there's a labor shortage. So if you look at from a historical standpoint, this is the absolute worst time to ever try to do an infrastructure bill. Not only does this infrastructure bill not have a lot of infrastructure, not only does it have zero transparency and where the infrastructure money's going. It also, you're not going to get a lot of infrastructure for your dollar for the 10% of projects that are road and bridge project. We're not going to get very many road and bridge because The cost of asphalt is crippled. The cost of rebar, the cost of concrete. The labor is going to be dubbed everything cost more. And you're just making a situation with government spending more money where there's going to be more inflation and more inflation. And it's just, it's frustrating as a fiscal conservative to see the money that's being wasted up here. That infrastructure bill",
