    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "No, not yet. But you know, the problem is it wouldn't, it wouldn't pass today. It would not pass. But these new members that are coming in, these new Democrats are getting elected in their 30s and early 40s, they're passionate about it. This is like their main thing. So you see a trend, the future people that are the future leaders that are coming to Washington, the younger ones, they're very passionate about this, which means it's going to be a priority once they become the majority. And, you know, another thing that hurts your Green New Deal now is people are frustrated because gas prices and natural gas prices and every type of energy, a skyrocketing right now. The administration doesn't have a lot of credibility to be able to pass and make your bill like, like the Green New Deal. But what you're seeing is through the executive order process, like Cancer and the Keystone Pipeline, they're already taking steps to initiate the Green New Deal. They just, instead of passing one big bowl bill, they're going to do executive orders. They're going to do everything they can, put a little language in this bill, a little language in that bill. And we're going to wake up in a few years and say, oh my gosh, they've already passed the green field. And that's why people need to be concerned about that.",
