    "turn_text": "I think the result of a majority of his policies basically spending too much money. We didn't need a stimulus bill in March and they passed that stimulus bill. During the last year of the Trump administration, Congress really passed too much stimulus. If the government had gotten out of the way, You wouldn't have needed all this. So the government forcing people to shut down initially, the Trump administration made the decision to shut something down. And then they realized, you know, we can't do that. It's bad, but it's not, you know, going to wipe the population of the planet out. But then you had liberal governors like Andy Beshear that kept on and then Gavin Newsom in California. We're going to keep you shut down. Restaurants can't have anybody in there. And they really got dramatic and overplayed their hand, right? Hurt economy, the more. So But Biden passed a huge stimulus bill, big giveaway in March. Then they've done this infrastructure bill. Now they're working on this bill back better, which is social spending, 100% unnecessary spending. And that's leading to even more inflation. I mean, we have bad inflation. Now it's going to get worse. And the thing about inflation, I tell everybody says, inflation's a hidden tax, it is. And they say it's a tax on the board. It absolutely is a tax on the board. You're talking about Dollar Tree, raising their process 25%. That's a pretty big hit for people who are struggling to get back. But inflation, the thing they don't talk about, inflation is great for the rich. If you have a lot of assets, if you have a big chunk of land somewhere, your land is going to ride that inflation way. So your land, you know, if you've got a farm worth $100,000 and there's 20% inflation, it's worth $120,000, right? That's good for you. But it's terrible for the person who's shopping at Dollar Tree, just trying to get enough groceries and supplies to get their family through the week. And even though Joe Biden and the Democrat tried to say they're doing policies to help the poor, they're doing policies that are devastating to the poor. Their policies are going to make the poor poor and the rich, rich. And that's something that people don't think about when they look at inflation.",
